        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="n-warn" parent="1" style="text;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;fontSize=12;fontColor=#8A5A00;whiteSpace=wrap;rounded=1;arcSize=6;strokeColor=#E0A800;strokeWidth=2;fillColor=#FFF9E6;spacing=12;" value="⚠&amp;nbsp; &lt;b&gt;This context is not deployed by the CDK app.&lt;/b&gt; There is no &lt;i&gt;NotificationStack&lt;/i&gt; in &lt;i&gt;infra/&lt;/i&gt; and no matching construct. The service provisions its own queue and tables at runtime (&lt;i&gt;ensureResources&lt;/i&gt; in resources.go), which works in the Aspire-orchestrated local environment — but means that on real AWS nothing here is created by &lt;i&gt;cdk deploy&lt;/i&gt;. Worth deciding whether it joins the CDK or is intentionally development-only." vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="80" width="910" x="60" y="105" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
